PowerShellGet is the native package manager for PowerShell. 
It has been mostly replaced by Microsoft.PowerShell.PSResourceGet

PowerShellGet provides the cmdlets needed to discover, install, update, 
and publish PowerShell artifacts like modules, scripts, 
and DSC (Desired State Configuration) resources.

Find-Module: Searches online repositories (like the PowerShell Gallery) for tools.
Install-Module: Downloads and installs a module onto your local machine.
Update-Module: Grabs the newest version of an installed module.
Uninstall-Module Safely removes a module from your system paths.









